{{- /*
  support/slack-tools — the "Slack tools (names vary by MCP server)"
  paragraph that every support prompt opens with. Standardises the
  invariant framing ("Match Slack MCP tools by capability, not exact
  name") and lets each caller drop in its own capability list.

  Fields on the `dict` argument:

    Capabilities:  a caller-supplied sentence(s) describing what
                   the caller needs Slack MCP tools for (verbs like
                   "read a thread's replies", "read recent channel
                   history", "post a reply to a thread", etc.).
                   The fragment renders this verbatim after the
                   stable "Match by capability..." lead-in.

    NoPosting:     when true, adds a trailing sentence noting that
                   no posting tool is needed for this prompt. Every
                   read-only support prompt sets this. Set false for
                   prompts that DO post (reply-to-user, gather-info,
                   continue-conversation).

    ReadMetadata:  when true, adds the "Read the target channel and
                   parent thread_ts from the bead metadata
                   (`slack_channel` / `slack_thread_ts`)" trailer.
                   Every per-bead prompt sets this; list-level and
                   channel-level prompts (housekeeping, watch-channel,
                   continue-conversation) set it false.

  Usage:

      {{ template "support/shared/slack-tools" (dict
         "Capabilities" "Here you only need to **read a thread's replies** (e.g. `slack_get_thread_replies*`, `conversations_replies_slack`)."
         "NoPosting" true
         "ReadMetadata" true) }}

  Whitespace: fragment body starts and ends flush at column 1 with
  no leading/trailing newline; callers use plain `{{ template ... }}`
  (no trim markers) inside their own `## Slack tools ...` heading
  section.
*/ -}}
{{- $caps := .Capabilities -}}
{{- $noPosting := .NoPosting -}}
{{- $readMeta := .ReadMetadata -}}
Match Slack MCP tools **by capability, not exact name**. {{ $caps }}
{{- if $readMeta }} Read the target channel and parent `thread_ts` from the bead metadata (`slack_channel` / `slack_thread_ts`).{{- end }}
{{- if $noPosting }} No posting tool is needed — this prompt never posts.{{- end }}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
